  /pages/llms is an llms.txt-style index of the site for language models.

  It is a theme template, not page content: the Shopify page's body is empty, so
  everything a crawler sees comes from this file. The suffix was set on the page
  but the template was never ported to Horizon, so from the theme swap until
  2026-10-20 the page fell back to templates/page.json and served four
  characters -- an <h1> reading "llms" and nothing else.

  Ported verbatim from the previous theme (147508887743,
  templates/page.llms.liquid) with one correction: collections/all is titled
  "All Products" and holds merch and gear as well as coffee, so calling it the
  master coffee collection pointed models at the wrong taxonomy.

  Every link below was checked against the shop on 2026-10-20: all fourteen
  collection handles resolve, and every /pages/ and /blogs/ path is published.
  Re-check them when the navigation changes -- a dead link here is worse than no
  file, because it is read by machines that will not notice.
{% endcomment %}
